                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="631-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>Cascade Microphones VIN-JET</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Bidirectional Ribbon Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Cascade VIN-JET is a long-format, passive ribbon microphone manufactured in China and upgraded in the US. </p><p>The single ribbon is made of 99% pure aluminum and measures approximately 5mm by 62mm. Suspended between Neodymium magnets, it produces an extended figure-of-8 pickup pattern with high (165dB) SPL capability.</p><p>Two models are available:</p><ul><li>VIN-JET - with stock transformer, $199</li><li>VIN-JET-L - with Lundahl LL2913 transformer, $349</li></ul><p>Both ship with a suspension shockmount, a padded storage pouch, an aluminum flight case, and a micro-fiber cleaning cloth.</p><p>The Cascade Vin-Jet (w/Lundahl upgrade) was part of our <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/2011/07/11/60000-ribbon-mic-shootout/" target="blank">$60,000 Ribbon Mic Shootout</a>.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Cascade/VIN-JET">Cascade Microphones VIN-JET</a> is also known as: VINJET.</p>
